# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  88mph-mass-appraisal — .gitignore
#
#  This is a PUBLIC repository about property records.
#  Nothing secret and nothing real belongs in a commit.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds real API keys (HuggingFace, Tavily, Anthropic).
# .env.example IS committed — it lists the variable NAMES only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.toml
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ── Python environment ───────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.Python

# uv writes the resolved lockfile — DO commit uv.lock so every
# attendee gets byte-identical package versions.
# (no entry here on purpose — this comment is the documentation)

# ── Jupyter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: we deliberately COMMIT notebook outputs so the repo is
# readable on GitHub without running anything, and so a dead
# cell can be narrated from the saved result on stage.
# Only the checkpoint scratch files are ignored.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# ── Model weights & caches ───────────────────────────────────
# Multi-gigabyte files. Attendees download these themselves.
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
models/
.cache/
hf_cache/
huggingface/
.locks/

# ── RAG / vector store artifacts ─────────────────────────────
# Rebuildable from data/ — never commit the index itself.
*.faiss
*.index
chroma/
.chroma/
vectorstore/
storage/

# ── Real property data (NEVER commit) ────────────────────────
# All demo data must be synthetic. Real parcels, owner names,
# and addresses stay out of this repo permanently.
data/real/
data/private/
data/**/*_real.*
*.mdb
*.accdb

# ── OS & editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# VS Code: ignore personal state, but SHARE the two files that make
# this repo open correctly on someone else's machine.
#
# Note the `/*`. Writing `.vscode/` here instead would break the
# negations below it: git does not look inside an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so a file within one can never be re-included. Excluding the
# directory's CONTENTS leaves the door open.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── Logs & temp ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Working notes — kept out of a clone, kept in history ─────
# CLAUDE.md is the engineering working agreement and FINDINGS.md is the
# measurement log behind it. Both are genuinely useful, and both are
# deliberately NOT shipped in a clone: somebody who clones this repo should
# see the demos, not four large documents about how they were built.
#
# They are NOT secret and were never removed from git history. To read them:
#     git log --all --oneline -- CLAUDE.md
#     git show <commit>:CLAUDE.md
#
# ⚠️ Claude Code reads CLAUDE.md from the working directory, so ignoring it
# here does not stop it working locally — but a FRESH CLONE will not have it.
# Recover it from history (above) before starting work on a new machine.
CLAUDE.md
FINDINGS.md

# ── Local-only working folders ───────────────────────────────
# Never shipped. Scratch space for planning and progress notes.
Tracking/
Plans/

# ── Scratch & backups ────────────────────────────────────────
scratchpad/
notes/
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ── Streamlit runtime ────────────────────────────────────────
# Same pattern as .vscode above: exclude the CONTENTS so the negation
# works, and share only the one file that makes the apps behave the same
# way on everybody's machine.
.streamlit/*
!.streamlit/config.toml

# ── More OS & tooling noise ──────────────────────────────────
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints
